{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports a [validation error](running-criteria.md#habeas-req-requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ValidationError).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged this from the supplied test sources only. I did not request any implementation source.\n\n**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.execute`:**\n1. `Criterion::execute` runs with a `ValidationContext` for the criterion's source node.\n2. It returns a `Send` future.\n3. An `Ok` value is the completed answer of type `Self::Ok`. That answer includes a negative assessment, and the answer is serializable.\n4. An `Err` value reports a `ValidationError<D::Error>`.\n\n**Test mapping:**\n- **Context for the source node, and `Ok` as the completed answer**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` runs a real criterion through `verify`. It asserts the output (`result` false, rationale \"ordinary computation\"). It then stores the evidence and checks that the saved dependency is `Node(1)` with the expected fingerprint. This shows the context was bound to the source node.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` defines a custom criterion whose `execute` reads `cx.node_id()`. It asserts that `false` is an `Ok` completed answer with the node dependency recorded. It then stores that answer and checks that the stored output is `json!(false)`.\n  - `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` covers a negative determination as a completed answer. It stores the answer and reloads it, and the reloaded output equals the original.\n- **`Err` reports a `ValidationError`**\n  - The decode-error test asserts that invalid input yields `ValidationError::Output` with `is_syntax()`, and that nothing is stored.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` asserts `Graph(\"missing\")` when a callback read fails, and that no record is stored.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` asserts `NoAgentConfigured` from `execute` and that nothing is stored.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` asserts `ValidationError::Agent(_)`.\n  - `validation_tests.rs#fn[agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload]` checks the `Agent` payload and display, and the `Graph` error source.\n- **`Send` future and serializable `Ok`**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` drives verify, store, load and refresh through a `send(...)` bound. The bound checks at compile time that the future is `Send`. The test also round-trips the answer through storage (17 reloaded as 17).\n\n**Gaps:** I found none. Each clause has a test that exercises it and asserts the outcome. The success path, the negative-answer-is-`Ok` case and the several error variants are all asserted. The `Send` requirement is enforced at compile time by the contracts test.",
